   "name": "Polyatomic ions",
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "A polyatomic ion is a charged group of atoms, like NH₄⁺, OH⁻, NO₃⁻, SO₄²⁻ and PO₄³⁻. To write a formula, criss-cross the valences as before. Put the ion in brackets when it gets a subscript other than 1: ammonium sulfate is (NH₄)₂SO₄."
    }
